{
  "case": "release notes from merged PRs",
  "variant": "without",
  "trial": 3,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 entry to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. The version and date come from `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE`.\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove the deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 responses with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nI matched the format of the earlier entries: issue IDs in parentheses and no author names. ACME-421 is marked with `!` in the PR list, so I put it first and labelled it as breaking. Each PR is listed separately and none were left out.\n\n**Decision for you:** this release contains a breaking change, but `VERSION` says 2.4.0, which is a minor bump. If you follow semantic versioning, removing `--legacy` would normally mean releasing 3.0.0. If you'd rather stay on 2.4.0, it's worth telling users of `sync --legacy` how to migrate. I left the version as it is; tell me if you want it changed.",
